  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member, I want the Messages list (« Tous », « MP », « MP multiples ») shown as one list on one screen, without page buttons or a page number, as in the current app.\n\n### Legacy, checked @ 87fe0d1c\n\n- `HFRswift/Swift/MPListView.swift:235-300` (`MPListViewModel.load`): a single `topicsLoader.fetchTopics`; no page state, no next or previous page, no pager in the view.\n- `Classes/ObjCMPTopicsLoaderWorker.m:9-15`: it always requests `/forum1.php?config=hfr.inc&cat=prive&page=1`, with `firstPageNumber = lastPageNumber = 1` and no next or previous URL.\n- So the current app shows **page 1 of the MP list only**, as one list. The « ⚑ n / m » on a row is the thread's own read page (`MPListView.swift:780-782`), not the list's page.\n\n### Wanted (operator, 2026-11-16, beta feedback)\n\n- SwiftHFR does the same for « Tous », « MP » and « MP multiples » (#899): one list, page 1 of `cat=prive`.\n- **Remove the page buttons** (‹ ›, first page) and the **« Page N » display** from the MP **list** views. The MP reader is unchanged (it keeps its page controls).\n- The row's « ⚑ lue / total » stays: it belongs to the thread.\n\n### Notes\n\n- #898 / PR #952 (mac/M1) changes when the pager shows on paged lists. The MP lists leave that set: coordinate so #952 does not re-add a pager there.\n- Known limit, as in the current app: conversations beyond the list's page 1 are not listed. Record it as parity in the gap report if a GAP row covers the MP list.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] No pager and no page number on the three MP list views; one fetch of page 1.\n- [ ] A test fails without the change: the MP list model requests page 1 only and exposes no paging state.\n- [ ] Device check in the general review.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
